.com/users/elliotfontaine/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotfontaine/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotfontaine/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotfontaine/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotfontaine/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elliotfontaine/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-11T15:17:37Z","updated_at":"2026-09-11T15:17:37Z","body":"My plugin was relying on this undocumented \"feature\" (or bug), as it makes extensive use of const members to avoid polluting the user's namespace with `class_name` classes.\r\n\r\nSo, for what it's worth, I think the `breaks compat` label is warranted, and this change should be mentioned in the migration guide.\r\n\r\nSee https://github.com/elliotfontaine/yard-godot/pull/123","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5636620006/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5682210485","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121171#issuecomment-5682210485","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121171","id":5682210485,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUq-mtQ","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-15T14:41:20Z","updated_at":"2026-09-15T14:41:20Z","body":"First of all thanks for keeping the global scope clear, always appreciate plugins that do that!\r\n\r\nInheritance by path (`extends \"res://my_script.gd\".Inner`) should be able to represent all valid usecases of inheriting from inner constants. Using constants to type other stuff should also be untouched by this change.\r\n\r\nFixing the edge cases of this pattern would have been very involved compared to just forbidding it flat out. Sorry for the code churn on your end!\r\n\r\n> So, for what it's worth, I think the `breaks compat` label is warranted, and this change should be mentioned in the migration guide.\r\n\r\nI don't think the migration guide for 4.8 exists yet, but the PR is listed in our documentation tracking. So if everything goes well it should be in there eventually.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5682210485/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]